 ## Overview
-This method estimates the positional error introduced by linear interpolation when determining the intersection of a scalar field with an isovalue on a grid edge. It leverages Taylor series expansion to bound the difference between the true root and the linear approximation without solving a linear system [S1]. It distinguishes itself from [Linear Edge Intersection](868-linear-edge-intersection.md) by providing a quantitative error metric rather than just the position, and from [Iterative Bisection Intersection Refinement](880-iterative-bisection-intersection-refinement.md) by offering an analytical estimate rather than a numerical refinement [S1].
